---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Tracker from '../../components/islands/Tracker';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { breadcrumbList, siteUrl } from '../../lib/seo';

const ghosts = await getCollection('ghosts');
const ghostInputs = [...ghosts]
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.number - b.data.number)
  .map((ghost) => ({
    slug: ghost.data.slug,
    name: ghost.data.name,
    number: ghost.data.number,
    evidence: ghost.data.evidence,
    extraEvidence: ghost.data.extraEvidence,
    guaranteedEvidence: ghost.data.guaranteedEvidence,
  }));

const base = siteUrl(Astro.site);
const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'DEAD AIR Evidence Tracker',
    applicationCategory: 'GameApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    description:
      'Narrow Phasmophobia ghost candidates by confirmed and ruled-out evidence across normal, nightmare, insanity, and custom difficulties.',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  },
  breadcrumbList([
    { name: 'DEAD AIR', url: `${base}/` },
    { name: 'Evidence tracker', url: Astro.url.href },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Phasmophobia Evidence Tracker — Narrow Ghost Candidates | DEAD AIR"
  description="Interactive Phasmophobia evidence tracker. Select confirmed and ruled-out evidence, apply Nightmare or Insanity rules, and see which ghosts remain."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">DEAD AIR</a> / Tools / Evidence tracker</p>
      <h1>Evidence tracker</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Confirm what you have found, rule out what you have not, and let the difficulty rules
        handle the rest. The tracker accounts for forced evidence and The Mimic's extra Ghost Orbs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <Tracker ghosts={ghostInputs} client:load />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="label">Normal</p>
          <h2>Three evidence</h2>
          <p>
            All evidence types can appear. A tool that gives no reading is real information: use
            the ruled-out state to remove ghosts that require it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="label">Nightmare and Insanity</p>
          <h2>Reduced evidence</h2>
          <p>
            One or two evidence types are hidden. Ruled-out evidence stops mattering because
            absence proves nothing, but forced evidence still appears for five ghosts.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <p class="label">Custom</p>
          <h2>Zero to three</h2>
          <p>
            Set how many evidence types are shown. At zero, only behavior can identify the ghost,
            and The Mimic still always shows Ghost Orbs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container ghost-content">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>How the candidate list works</h2>
        <p>
          Each ghost has three evidence types. On reduced difficulties, the game hides some of
          them, so the tracker considers every combination the ghost could still show. A ghost
          remains a candidate if all of your confirmed evidence fits one of those combinations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Five ghosts keep a guaranteed evidence type: Hantu keeps Freezing Temperatures, Goryo
          keeps D.O.T.S. Projector, Obake keeps Ultraviolet, and both Moroi and Deogen keep Spirit
          Box. The Mimic is the exception on the other side: it always shows Ghost Orbs in addition
          to its three main evidence types, even when the difficulty hides other evidence.
        </p>
        <h2>Reading the result</h2>
        <p>
          The list is a shortlist, not a verdict. Behavior, hunt speed, and ability tests still
          separate ghosts that share evidence. Open any candidate to see its identification tests,
          and use the <a href="/ghost-cheat-sheet/">cheat sheet</a> when you want the full matrix.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="panel ghost-aside">
        <p class="label">Rules applied</p>
        <h2>Difficulty checklist</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Normal: all three evidence types, ruled-out readings count.</li>
          <li>Nightmare: two shown, one hidden.</li>
          <li>Insanity: one shown, two hidden.</li>
          <li>Custom: zero to three shown.</li>
          <li>Forced evidence stays visible for five ghosts.</li>
          <li>The Mimic always adds Ghost Orbs.</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn mt-2" href="/ghost-cheat-sheet/">Open the cheat sheet</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container faq-layout">
      <div>
      <h2>Tracker questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Does the tracker save my progress?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. The current mode and evidence selections are stored in your browser and encoded in
            the page URL, so you can bookmark or share a hunt.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Why can I not rule out evidence on Nightmare or Insanity?</summary>
          <p>
            Reduced difficulties hide evidence. A tool that shows nothing may simply have that
            evidence hidden, so treating absence as proof would remove the correct ghost.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How does The Mimic appear?</summary>
          <p>
            The Mimic always shows Ghost Orbs on top of its three main evidence types. The tracker
            adds those orbs automatically in every mode, including custom runs with zero main
            evidence shown.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What if no ghosts remain?</summary>
          <p>
            Recheck each reading and the difficulty mode. A single mistaken ruled-out entry in
            normal difficulty can eliminate the correct ghost.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="panel">
        <p class="label">Before you commit</p>
        <h2>Check the behavior</h2>
        <p>Shared evidence creates shortlists, not verdicts. Open a candidate and verify its ability, hunt speed, and weakness.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/ghosts/">Browse ghost entries</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
